; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#cer-host-ip-address-per-address)
; AVP: Host-IP-Address
; Command: Capabilities-Exchange-Request
; Section: 5.3.1
; Page: 62
"When Diameter is run over SCTP [RFC4960] or DTLS/SCTP [RFC6083], which allow for connections to span multiple interfaces and multiple IP addresses, the Capabilities-Exchange-Request message MUST contain one Host-IP-Address AVP for each potential IP address that MAY be locally used when transmitting Diameter messages."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#cea-host-ip-address-per-address)
; AVP: Host-IP-Address
; Command: Capabilities-Exchange-Answer
; Section: 5.3.2
; Page: 63
"When Diameter is run over SCTP [RFC4960] or DTLS/SCTP [RFC6083], which allow connections to span multiple interfaces, hence, multiple IP addresses, the Capabilities-Exchange-Answer message MUST contain one Host-IP-Address AVP for each potential IP address that MAY be locally used when transmitting Diameter messages."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#supported-vendor-id-not-zero)
; AVP: Supported-Vendor-Id
; Section: 5.3.6
; Page: 64
"The value of this AVP MUST NOT be set to zero."
    exclude 0


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Disconnect-Cause
; Section: 5.4.3
; Page: 66
Disconnect-Cause ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 273 >
        REBOOTING                  = 0
        BUSY                       = 1
        DO_NOT_WANT_TO_TALK_TO_YOU = 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#cer-destination-realm-not-proxiable)
; AVP: Destination-Realm
; Command: Capabilities-Exchange-Request
; Section: 6.1
; Page: 74
"A request that is not able to be proxied (such as a CER) MUST NOT contain either Destination-Realm or Destination-Host AVPs."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#cer-destination-host-not-proxiable)
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Command: Capabilities-Exchange-Request
; Section: 6.1
; Page: 74
"A request that is not able to be proxied (such as a CER) MUST NOT contain either Destination-Realm or Destination-Host AVPs."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#dpr-destination-realm-not-proxiable)
; AVP: Destination-Realm
; Command: Disconnect-Peer-Request
; Section: 6.1
; Page: 74
"A request that is not able to be proxied (such as a CER) MUST NOT contain either Destination-Realm or Destination-Host AVPs."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#dpr-destination-host-not-proxiable)
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Command: Disconnect-Peer-Request
; Section: 6.1
; Page: 74
"A request that is not able to be proxied (such as a CER) MUST NOT contain either Destination-Realm or Destination-Host AVPs."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#dwr-destination-realm-not-proxiable)
; AVP: Destination-Realm
; Command: Device-Watchdog-Request
; Section: 6.1
; Page: 74
"A request that is not able to be proxied (such as a CER) MUST NOT contain either Destination-Realm or Destination-Host AVPs."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#dwr-destination-host-not-proxiable)
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Command: Device-Watchdog-Request
; Section: 6.1
; Page: 74
"A request that is not able to be proxied (such as a CER) MUST NOT contain either Destination-Realm or Destination-Host AVPs."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#answer-session-id-the-requests)
; AVP: Session-Id
; Messages: answers
; Section: 6.2
; Page: 80
"If the Session-Id is present in the request, it MUST be included in the answer."
    present-if request/Session-Id
    equals request/Session-Id


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#answer-proxy-info-the-requests)
; AVP: Proxy-Info
; Messages: answers
; Section: 6.2
; Page: 80
"Any Proxy-Info AVPs in the request MUST be added to the answer message, in the same order they were present in the request."
    present-if request/Proxy-Info


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#destination-host-agent-initiated)
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Section: 6.5
; Page: 82
"This AVP MUST be present in all unsolicited agent initiated messages, MAY be present in request messages, and MUST NOT be present in answer messages."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#answer-destination-host-absent)
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Messages: answers
; Section: 6.5
; Page: 82
"This AVP MUST be present in all unsolicited agent initiated messages, MAY be present in request messages, and MUST NOT be present in answer messages."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#answer-destination-realm-absent)
; AVP: Destination-Realm
; Messages: answers
; Section: 6.6
; Page: 82
"The Destination-Realm AVP MUST NOT be present in answer messages."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#route-record-the-peers-origin-host)
; AVP: Route-Record
; Section: 6.7.1
; Page: 83
"The identity added in this AVP MUST be the same as the one received in the Origin-Host of the Capabilities Exchange message."
    text-only


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Proxy-Info
; Section: 6.7.2
; Page: 83
Proxy-Info ::= < AVP header: 284 >
        { Proxy-Host }
        { Proxy-State }
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#auth-application-id-the-headers)
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Section: 6.8
; Page: 83
"If present in a message other than CER and CEA, the value of the Auth-Application-Id AVP MUST match the Application Id present in the Diameter message header."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#acct-application-id-the-headers)
; AVP: Acct-Application-Id
; Section: 6.9
; Page: 84
"If present in a message other than CER and CEA, the value of the Acct-Application-Id AVP MUST match the Application Id present in the Diameter message header."
    text-only


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: Inband-Security-Id
; Kind: values
; Section: 6.10
; Page: 84
NO_INBAND_SECURITY = 0
TLS                = 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#inband-security-id-default)
; AVP: Inband-Security-Id
; Section: 6.10
; Page: 84
"NO_INBAND_SECURITY 0"
"This peer does not support TLS/TCP and DTLS/SCTP. This is the default value, if the AVP is omitted."
    default NO_INBAND_SECURITY


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Vendor-Specific-Application-Id
; Section: 6.11
; Page: 84
Vendor-Specific-Application-Id ::= < AVP header: 260 >
        { Vendor-Id }
        [ Auth-Application-Id ]
        [ Acct-Application-Id ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#vendor-specific-application-id-one-application)
; AVP: Vendor-Specific-Application-Id
; Section: 6.11
; Page: 84
"A Vendor-Specific-Application-Id AVP MUST contain exactly one of either Auth-Application-Id or Acct-Application-Id."
    members at-least-one Auth-Application-Id Acct-Application-Id
"It MUST also match the Application Id present in the Diameter header except when used in a CER or CEA message."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#vendor-specific-application-id-not-both)
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Within: Vendor-Specific-Application-Id
; Section: 6.11
; Page: 84
"A Vendor-Specific-Application-Id AVP MUST contain exactly one of either Auth-Application-Id or Acct-Application-Id."
    excludes Acct-Application-Id


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#redirect-host-redirect-indication)
; AVP: Redirect-Host
; Messages: answers
; Section: 6.12
; Page: 85
"One or more instances of this AVP MUST be present if the answer message's 'E' bit is set and the Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_REDIRECT_INDICATION."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_REDIRECT_INDICATION


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Redirect-Host-Usage
; Section: 6.13
; Page: 85
Redirect-Host-Usage ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 261 >
        DONT_CACHE            = 0
        ALL_SESSION           = 1
        ALL_REALM             = 2
        REALM_AND_APPLICATION = 3
        ALL_APPLICATION       = 4
        ALL_HOST              = 5
        ALL_USER              = 6


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#redirect-max-cache-time-redirect-indication)
; AVP: Redirect-Max-Cache-Time
; Messages: answers
; Section: 6.14
; Page: 87
"This AVP MUST be present in answer messages whose 'E' bit is set, whose Result-Code AVP is set to DIAMETER_REDIRECT_INDICATION, and whose Redirect-Host-Usage AVP set to a non-zero value."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_REDIRECT_INDICATION and Redirect-Host-Usage and not Redirect-Host-Usage = DONT_CACHE


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: Result-Code
; Kind: result-codes
; Section: 7.1
; Page: 89
DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH          = 1001 ; 7.1.1
DIAMETER_SUCCESS                   = 2001 ; 7.1.2
DIAMETER_LIMITED_SUCCESS           = 2002 ; 7.1.2
DIAMETER_COMMAND_UNSUPPORTED       = 3001 ; 7.1.3
DIAMETER_UNABLE_TO_DELIVER         = 3002 ; 7.1.3
DIAMETER_REALM_NOT_SERVED          = 3003 ; 7.1.3
DIAMETER_TOO_BUSY                  = 3004 ; 7.1.3
DIAMETER_LOOP_DETECTED             = 3005 ; 7.1.3
DIAMETER_REDIRECT_INDICATION       = 3006 ; 7.1.3
DIAMETER_APPLICATION_UNSUPPORTED   = 3007 ; 7.1.3
DIAMETER_INVALID_HDR_BITS          = 3008 ; 7.1.3
DIAMETER_INVALID_AVP_BITS          = 3009 ; 7.1.3
DIAMETER_UNKNOWN_PEER              = 3010 ; 7.1.3
DIAMETER_AUTHENTICATION_REJECTED   = 4001 ; 7.1.4
DIAMETER_OUT_OF_SPACE              = 4002 ; 7.1.4
ELECTION_LOST                      = 4003 ; 7.1.4
DIAMETER_AVP_UNSUPPORTED           = 5001 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_UNKNOWN_SESSION_ID        = 5002 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_AUTHORIZATION_REJECTED    = 5003 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_INVALID_AVP_VALUE         = 5004 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_MISSING_AVP               = 5005 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_RESOURCES_EXCEEDED        = 5006 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_CONTRADICTING_AVPS        = 5007 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_AVP_NOT_ALLOWED           = 5008 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_AVP_OCCURS_TOO_MANY_TIMES = 5009 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_NO_COMMON_APPLICATION     = 5010 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_UNSUPPORTED_VERSION       = 5011 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_UNABLE_TO_COMPLY          = 5012 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_INVALID_BIT_IN_HEADER     = 5013 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_INVALID_AVP_LENGTH        = 5014 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_INVALID_MESSAGE_LENGTH    = 5015 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_INVALID_AVP_BIT_COMBO     = 5016 ; 7.1.5
DIAMETER_NO_COMMON_SECURITY        = 5017 ; 7.1.5


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#error-reporting-host-another-host)
; AVP: Error-Reporting-Host
; Section: 7.1
; Page: 89
"A non-successful Result-Code AVP (one containing a non-2xxx value other than DIAMETER_REDIRECT_INDICATION) MUST include the Error-Reporting-Host AVP if the host setting the Result-Code AVP is different from the identity encoded in the Origin-Host AVP."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#answer-failed-avp-with-the-error)
; AVP: Failed-AVP
; Messages: answers
; Section: 7.1.5
; Page: 92
"DIAMETER_AVP_UNSUPPORTED 5001"
"A Diameter message with this error MUST contain one or more Failed-AVP AVPs containing the AVPs that caused the failure."
"DIAMETER_INVALID_AVP_VALUE 5004"
"A Diameter message indicating this error MUST include the offending AVPs within a Failed-AVP AVP."
"DIAMETER_CONTRADICTING_AVPS 5007"
"The Failed-AVP AVP MUST be present, which contain the AVPs that contradicted each other."
"DIAMETER_AVP_NOT_ALLOWED 5008"
"The Failed-AVP AVP MUST be included and contain a copy of the offending AVP."
"DIAMETER_AVP_OCCURS_TOO_MANY_TIMES 5009"
"The Failed-AVP AVP MUST be included and contain a copy of the first instance of the offending AVP that exceeded the maximum number of occurrences."
"DIAMETER_INVALID_AVP_LENGTH 5014"
"DIAMETER_INVALID_AVP_BIT_COMBO 5016"
    present-if Result-Code in DIAMETER_AVP_UNSUPPORTED,
        DIAMETER_INVALID_AVP_VALUE, DIAMETER_CONTRADICTING_AVPS,
        DIAMETER_AVP_NOT_ALLOWED, DIAMETER_AVP_OCCURS_TOO_MANY_TIMES,
        DIAMETER_INVALID_AVP_LENGTH, DIAMETER_INVALID_AVP_BIT_COMBO


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#error-reporting-host-a-failure)
; AVP: Error-Reporting-Host
; Section: 7.4
; Page: 96
"This AVP contains the identity of the Diameter host that sent the Result-Code AVP to a value other than 2001 (Success), only if the host setting the Result-Code is different from the one encoded in the Origin-Host AVP. This AVP is intended to be used for troubleshooting purposes, and it MUST be set when the Result-Code AVP indicates a failure."
    text-only


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Failed-AVP
; Section: 7.5
; Page: 96
Failed-AVP ::= < AVP header: 279 >
     1* { AVP }


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Experimental-Result
; Section: 7.6
; Page: 97
Experimental-Result ::= < AVP header: 297 >
        { Vendor-Id }
        { Experimental-Result-Code }


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#authorization-lifetime-extendable)
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Section: 8
; Page: 98
"When a Diameter server authorizes a user to implement network resources for a finite amount of time, and it is willing to extend the authorization via a future request, it MUST add the Authorization- Lifetime AVP to the answer message."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#auth-session-state-not-in-re-authorization)
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Section: 8
; Page: 98
"Note that the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED MUST NOT be set in subsequent re-authorization requests and answers."
    text-only


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Auth-Request-Type
; Section: 8.7
; Page: 116
Auth-Request-Type ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 274 >
        AUTHENTICATE_ONLY      = 1
        AUTHORIZE_ONLY         = 2
        AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE = 3


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#session-id-the-senders-identity)
; AVP: Session-Id
; Section: 8.8
; Page: 116
"The Session-Id MUST begin with the sender's identity encoded in the DiameterIdentity type (see Section 4.3.1). The remainder of the Session-Id is delimited by a \";\" character"
    encoding session-id
"All messages pertaining to a specific session MUST include only one Session-Id AVP, and the same value MUST be used throughout the life of a session."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#authorization-lifetime-not-above-the-timeout)
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Section: 8.9
; Page: 117
"If both this AVP and the Session-Timeout AVP are present in a message, the value of the latter MUST NOT be smaller than the Authorization-Lifetime AVP."
    text-only
"The server MUST return a value that is equal to, or smaller than, the one provided by the client."
    text-only


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Auth-Session-State
; Section: 8.11
; Page: 118
Auth-Session-State ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 277 >
        STATE_MAINTAINED    = 0
        NO_STATE_MAINTAINED = 1


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Re-Auth-Request-Type
; Section: 8.12
; Page: 118
Re-Auth-Request-Type ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 285 >
        AUTHORIZE_ONLY         = 0
        AUTHORIZE_AUTHENTICATE = 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#re-auth-request-type-with-a-lifetime)
; AVP: Re-Auth-Request-Type
; Section: 8.12
; Page: 118
"If the answer message contains an Authorization-Lifetime AVP with a positive value, the Re-Auth-Request-Type AVP MUST be present in an answer message."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#session-timeout-not-below-the-lifetime)
; AVP: Session-Timeout
; Section: 8.13
; Page: 119
"When both the Session-Timeout and the Authorization-Lifetime AVPs are present in an answer message, the former MUST be equal to or greater than the value of the latter."
    text-only


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Termination-Cause
; Section: 8.15
; Page: 120
; Values: the IANA registry for Termination-Cause AVP Values [IANATCV]
Termination-Cause ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 295 >
      ; RESERVED                      = 0 ;; supplied: (RFC6733.py#termination-cause-values)
        DIAMETER_LOGOUT               = 1 ;; supplied: (RFC6733.py#termination-cause-values)
        DIAMETER_SERVICE_NOT_PROVIDED = 2 ;; supplied: (RFC6733.py#termination-cause-values)
        DIAMETER_BAD_ANSWER           = 3 ;; supplied: (RFC6733.py#termination-cause-values)
        DIAMETER_ADMINISTRATIVE       = 4 ;; supplied: (RFC6733.py#termination-cause-values)
        DIAMETER_LINK_BROKEN          = 5 ;; supplied: (RFC6733.py#termination-cause-values)
        DIAMETER_AUTH_EXPIRED         = 6 ;; supplied: (RFC6733.py#termination-cause-values)
        DIAMETER_USER_MOVED           = 7 ;; supplied: (RFC6733.py#termination-cause-values)
        DIAMETER_SESSION_TIMEOUT      = 8 ;; supplied: (RFC6733.py#termination-cause-values)


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#origin-state-id-higher-after-a-reset)
; AVP: Origin-State-Id
; Section: 8.16
; Page: 120
"A Diameter entity issuing this AVP MUST create a higher value for this AVP each time its state is reset."
    text-only


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: Session-Binding
; Kind: bits
; Section: 8.17
; Page: 120
RE_AUTH    = 0
STR        = 1
ACCOUNTING = 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#destination-host-session-binding)
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Section: 8.17
; Page: 120
"When set, future re-auth messages for this session MUST NOT include the Destination-Host AVP."
"When set, the STR message for this session MUST NOT include the Destination-Host AVP."
"When set, all accounting messages for this session MUST NOT include the Destination-Host AVP."
    text-only


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Session-Server-Failover
; Section: 8.18
; Page: 121
Session-Server-Failover ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 271 >
        REFUSE_SERVICE          = 0
        TRY_AGAIN               = 1
        ALLOW_SERVICE           = 2
        TRY_AGAIN_ALLOW_SERVICE = 3


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#class-in-later-messages)
; AVP: Class
; Section: 8.20
; Page: 122
"When one or more Class AVPs are present in application-specific authorization answer messages, they MUST be present in subsequent re-authorization, session termination and accounting messages."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#acr-user-name-available)
; AVP: User-Name
; Command: Accounting-Request
; Section: 9.5
; Page: 125
"In all accounting records, the Session-Id AVP MUST be present; the User-Name AVP MUST be present if it is available to the Diameter client."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#acr-accounting-record-type-the-service)
; AVP: Accounting-Record-Type
; Command: Accounting-Request
; Section: 9.5
; Page: 125
"If the accounted service is a one-time event, meaning that the start and stop of the event are simultaneous, then the Accounting-Record-Type AVP MUST be present and set to the value EVENT_RECORD."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#aca-session-id-the-requests)
; AVP: Session-Id
; Command: Accounting-Answer
; Section: 9.7.2
; Page: 128
"The Accounting-Answer command contains the same Session-Id as the corresponding request."
    equals request/Session-Id


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Accounting-Record-Type
; Section: 9.8.1
; Page: 129
Accounting-Record-Type ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 480 >
        EVENT_RECORD   = 1
        START_RECORD   = 2
        INTERIM_RECORD = 3
        STOP_RECORD    = 4


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#acct-multi-session-id-the-session-id-format)
; AVP: Acct-Multi-Session-Id
; Section: 9.8.5
; Page: 131
"The Acct-Multi-Session-Id AVP (AVP Code 50) is of type UTF8String, following the format specified in Section 8.8."
    encoding session-id


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (RFC6733.dadx#accounting-sub-session-id-increasing)
; AVP: Accounting-Sub-Session-Id
; Section: 9.8.6
; Page: 131
"The combination of the Session-Id and this AVP MUST be unique per sub-session, and the value of this AVP MUST be monotonically increased by one for all new sub-sessions."
    text-only


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Accounting-Realtime-Required
; Section: 9.8.7
; Page: 132
Accounting-Realtime-Required ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 483 >
        DELIVER_AND_GRANT = 1
        GRANT_AND_STORE   = 2
        GRANT_AND_LOSE    = 3


